title: Case Manager › Active cases › Being prepared card
route: /manager
intro: Above the tracker, one folded row says how many cases the agents are still preparing and how many need a person, and links to Authorizations. Opening it shows the full list, most urgent first, with four chips that narrow it by who has the next move, and 'sent today' that jumps to the Dashboard. The list is kept so the queue is not repeated on the page. Each row is explained in the next diagram.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open Case Manager (Active cases tab)"
screen sf "Folded row 'Being prepared' above the tracker (closed at first)\nSummary '5 being prepared, 3 need you'\nLink 'Open in Authorizations' and a chevron"
process pn "'N need you' counts cases with an open question, a signature to give, unfinished intake or an agent that could not finish: 3 at the start, the same cases as the two badges below\nWith page filters on: '1 of 5 match the filters, 1 needs you'. With none: 'Nothing is being prepared'"
click cl "Click 'Open in Authorizations'"
process pl "Go to /authorizations\n(Under 900 px wide the link moves inside the opened row)"
goto gl "Continues in: Authorizations › Queue › Open the queue and read the top"
click co "Click the header, or Tab to it and press Enter or Space"
screen sc "Opened: 'Most urgent first. Each case moves through eight steps; the agents do all but Ask and Sign.'"
process pc "Click the header again to fold it\nThe chip you picked stays while the page is open"
process p1 "Rows are the drafts that were saved and not yet sent\n5 at the start: R-1042, R-0988, I-2207, R-1101, I-2262"
process p2 "Search, level of care and payer from the filter bar narrow the rows\nThe tracker's status filter does not apply here"
screen sh "Top right of the opened row\nGhost button '4 sent today', then the chips 'All', 'Agents working', 'Needs your input', 'Ready to sign'"

click c1 "Click '4 sent today'"
process p3 "Go to /dashboard?stage=received"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Stage strip › Click a stage tile"
click c2 "Click a chip"
decision d1 "Which chip?"
process k1 "'All': every row"
process k2 "'Agents working': rows where agents are still running"
process k3 "'Needs your input': rows with an open question, or intake not finished\nBadge shows how many (2 at the start)"
process k4 "'Ready to sign': rows where every check passed\nBadge shows how many (1 at the start)"
process p4 "Rows narrow to that chip\nThe badge counts follow the page filters but not the chip itself"

process o1 "Order: rows that need a person come first (questions, signatures, unfinished intake)\nThen the earliest due date"
process o2 "At the start: R-1042, R-0988, I-2207, then R-1101, I-2262"

decision d2 "Are there rows to show?"
screen r1 "A column of case rows"
goto g2 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › One row and its button"
goto g3 "Continues in: Case Manager › Empty states › Nothing to show"
goto g4 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › A new case joins the tracker"
goto g5 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Updated for a payer change"
end e1 "Rows are on screen"

process p5 "After a case is signed and sent in New case it leaves this list, 'sent today' counts one more, and the tracker adds it as 'New today' unless it already had a row"
start s2 "Later: a case is signed and sent in New case › Review and sign"

s1 --> sf --> pn
sf --> cl --> pl --> gl
sf --> co --> sc --> p1 --> p2 --> sh
sc -.-> pc
sh --> c1 --> p3 --> g1
sh --> c2 --> d1
d1 -->|All| k1 --> p4
d1 -->|Working| k2 --> p4
d1 -->|Needs input| k3 --> p4
d1 -->|Ready| k4 --> p4
p4 --> o1
p2 --> o1
o1 --> o2 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| r1 --> g2
d2 -->|No| g3
r1 --> e1
s2 --> p5 --> p1
p5 --> g4
r1 -.-> g5
